{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.cb5bff4d6f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-170","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Adeyemi is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Adeyemi added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Because the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks, Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","Adeyemi found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Adeyemi concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
